  "narrative": "The new discovery batch adds one very large new association, one clearly meaningful moderate association, and several mostly null or imprecise probes. H49, TP53 loss versus dependency_USP7, has signed estimate +0.802 (CI +0.782 to +0.822), which is far beyond any plausible 10% clinical threshold for USP7-scale outcomes and also far beyond null. I accept this as a strong same-dataset association and keep it active while requesting independent validation because it is a new large finding and independent confirmation would be scientifically valuable. H54, the accepted KEAP1-loss association restricted to STK11-loss lines, has signed estimate +0.775 (CI +0.727 to +0.823), supporting persistence of the large weaker-NFE2L2 effect in this co-mutation context; because the main KEAP1 effect is already accepted and heavily checked, this robustness claim is accepted and closed. H59, CDKN2A loss versus dependency_MDM2, has signed estimate +0.117 (CI +0.082 to +0.152); the lower bound exceeds the approximate 0.026 absolute 10% threshold for MDM2-scale outcomes, so I accept it as a meaningful dataset association and keep it active for future technical and specificity checks. H16 is clinically insignificant for the TP53-loss direction on RPL11: signed estimate +0.004 with upper bound +0.024 below the approximate 0.025 RPL11 threshold, so I reject it. H57, H58, and H37 are signed negative or near-null; their positive claim-direction upper bounds are well below outcome-scale 10% thresholds, so the hypothesized directions are rejected, even though the intervals may allow some opposite-direction signal. H14, H52, H53, and H56 are near-null but their intervals include values around or slightly above the relevant 10% thresholds, so I leave them unresolved but closed as low-yield follow-up checks. H51 is a marker-null direct control for marker F and dependency_NFE2L2; it is reassuringly near-null, but the interval still permits marginal positive and negative differences, so it remains unresolved and closed as specificity evidence. I did not request validation for the huge accepted H54, nor for the rejected or low-yield unresolved claims. I registered same-dataset technical robustness, marker-null, and one TP53 interaction proposal for the newly accepted H49 and H59 effects. All conclusions remain associations in the supplied lung-lineage dataset, not causal or generalizable claims.",
